OVERVIEW: Display metadata from DICOM medical imaging files

Extracts and displays metadata tags from DICOM Part 10 files.
Supports multiple output formats for different use cases.

Examples:
  dicom-info scan.dcm
  dicom-info --format json report.dcm
  dicom-info --bounded-summary --format json scan.dcm
  dicom-info --tag PatientName --tag StudyDate exam.dcm

--tag takes a PS3.6 keyword (exact, e.g. PatientName), a tag (0010,0010), or
any part of a PS3.6 Attribute name (case-insensitive, e.g. "Patient").

USAGE: dicom-info <file-path> [--format <format>] [--tag <tag> ...] [--show-private] [--statistics] [--force] [--bounded-summary]

ARGUMENTS:
  <file-path>             Path to the DICOM file

OPTIONS:
  -f, --format <format>   Output format: text, json, csv (default: plain text
                          (default))
  -t, --tag <tag>         Filter by keyword, tag (GGGG,EEEE) or part of the
                          Attribute name (can be used multiple times)
  --show-private          Include private tags in output
  --statistics            Show file statistics
  --force                 Force parsing of files without DICM prefix
  --bounded-summary       Strictly parse verified source windows and report
                          source/index storage usage without displaying tag
                          values
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

